@page "/privacy"
@using MotiffLab.MusicCore.Analytics

<PageTitle>Privacy · Motiff Lab</PageTitle>

@* The privacy notice (#65, docs/01-mvp-stage-1.md: Content sources and rights). The analytics table is read from the catalogue, so it always matches what can be sent. *@
<main class="lab document">
    <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
    <p class="meta">Draft for the Stage 1 study, before legal review. Questions: ask the person who invited you to the study.</p>

    <h2>Your music stays on this device</h2>
    <p>
        Files you import, your projects, motifs and variations are read, analysed, changed and played in this browser,
        and saved in this browser's storage, with the variations and notes you keep about a phrase. Motiff Lab never
        uploads them. Exports (MIDI and project files) are saved straight to this device. To delete a project, use
        Delete on the home screen; clearing this site's data in the browser deletes everything.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
        The app is served by Microsoft Azure Static Web Apps. As with any website, the host processes your IP address
        to deliver the app's files. Motiff Lab adds no tracking to this and keeps no record of it. After the first
        visit the app works offline from this browser's cache.
    </p>

    <h2 id="analytics">Anonymous usage analytics</h2>
    <p>
        Analytics are off until you turn them on in <a href="settings">Settings</a>, and you can turn them off there at
        any time. When they are on, this browser gets a random ID, so that a week of use can be counted, and the app
        records the events below. They hold counts, yes-or-no answers and choices from fixed lists; never your music,
        file names, titles or any text you type. Turning analytics off deletes the ID and any events not yet sent.
    </p>
    <p>
        This version does not send analytics yet: events wait on this device, and Settings lists them. When sending
        starts, events will go to a Motiff Lab endpoint and be stored in Azure Table Storage in an EU region, without IP
        addresses; how long they are kept will be stated here before then. This version reports no errors.
    </p>
    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Event</th><th scope="col">What it holds</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            @foreach (string name in AnalyticsCatalogue.EventNames)
            {
                <tr>
                    <td><code>@name</code></td>
                    <td>@Describe(AnalyticsCatalogue.PropertiesOf(name))</td>
                </tr>
            }
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>AI assistance</h2>
    <p>
        AI assistance is not in this version. When it arrives it will be off until you turn it on, and a panel will
        show exactly what is sent: a short digest of facts about the motif you selected, never your file. It will be
        processed by Microsoft, as provider of Azure AI Foundry, in an EU region, and Motiff Lab will not store it. The
        provider's retention and abuse-monitoring terms for the deployment will be stated here before AI can be turned
        on. You will be able to turn it off in Settings at any time, and every feature works without it.
    </p>
</main>

@code {
    private static string Describe(IReadOnlyList<AnalyticsProperty> properties) => properties.Count == 0
        ? "Nothing but the event and the time."
        : string.Join("; ", properties.Select(property => property switch
        {
            CountProperty count => $"{count.Name}: a number from {count.Min} to {count.Max}",
            FlagProperty flag => $"{flag.Name}: yes or no",
            ChoiceProperty choice => $"{choice.Name}: one of {string.Join(", ", choice.Choices)}",
            _ => property.Name,
        }));
}
